body:
@justinmk I also happened segfault on f8f63393c1.
I didn't yet some debugging, but certainly that's problem when place sign(s).
Will more details comment and try to bisect.

Okay, there is most definitely something wrong with the structure of the linked list. Could not yet produce a segfault, but an endless loop (while executing with valgrind) at the exact same location. 

`  
while (prev != NULL && prev->lnum == lnum && prev->priority <= prio) {
    prev = prev->prev;
  }
`
With `prev->prev` pointing at `prev` itself.

Still my best guess a concurrent modification of the linked list. Can anyone with more knowledge in neovim internals answer the question if `ex_sign`, `f_sign_*` can be called in parallel? I don't know what thread architecture neovim has (digging around, but maybe someone is faster). 
And maybe someone can tell me what method neovim uses to guard critical sections against parallel execution, so I can place guards at `insert_sign` and `buf_delsign` and test again?
